    <x:String x:Key="Err_EngineExit_HintDllNotFound">Exit code 0xC0000135 means the Windows loader could not resolve a dependent DLL before engine.exe started — the engine never runs, so stdout/stderr stay empty and the UI cannot read the missing file name.&#x0a;&#x0a;• Often OpenSSL: copy libcrypto-3-x64.dll and libssl-3-x64.dll from your vcpkg installed\x64-windows\bin next to engine.exe (or run Build-Engine.ps1 — it copies them).&#x0a;• If the CRT is missing, install “Microsoft Visual C++ 2015–2022 Redistributable (x64)”. Debug builds may need MSVC on the machine.&#x0a;&#x0a;If you installed from a package, reinstall the application from the official installer so all component DLLs (for example next to engine.exe) are restored.</x:String>
